        "content": "<p>Hi, I'm happy to announce <strong>CCtx</strong>, a library providing first-class constructor contexts:</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/pandaman64/CCtx\">https://github.com/pandaman64/CCtx</a></p>\n<p>A constructor context represents a partially constructed value with one distinguished hole. It is useful for writing tail-recursive builders that accumulate constructor applications without growing the call stack.</p>\n<p>For example, here is a tail-recursive <code>List.map</code>, which accumulates the values at the end:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CCtx</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rec</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">go</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ctx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[],</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">acc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">acc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">++.</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">::</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">acc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">go</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">acc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">++</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">cctx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ys</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">::</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ys</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">go</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CCtx.empty</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The main operations are:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>cctx hole =&gt; body</code> constructs a context</li>\n<li><code>c ++. x</code> fills its hole</li>\n<li><code>c₁ ++ c₂</code> composes two contexts</li>\n<li><code>CCtx.empty</code> is the empty context</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The design follows Leijen and Lorenzen's <a href=\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3571233\">Tail Recursion Modulo Context</a>, which is also implemented in the Koka programming language. The library uses C FFI so that applying or composing an exclusively-used context updates it <strong>in-place</strong> in <strong>constant time</strong>, while reusing a context preserves value semantics by copying the constructor path. An elaborator for <code>cctx</code> wraps these unsafe FFI primitives and checks that contexts are well-formed; reviews of that part would be especially appreciated.</p>\n<p>Logically, <code>CCtx α β</code> denotes a function <code>β → α</code>, so contexts can also be reasoned about through <code>CCtx.toFun</code>.</p>\n<p>To try it, add:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"TOML\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">[[require]]</span>\n<span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"CCtx\"</span>\n<span class=\"n\">git</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"https://github.com/pandaman64/CCtx\"</span>\n<span class=\"n\">rev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"main\"</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Feedback, bug reports, and ideas for useful examples are very welcome!</p>",
